# L §6.1: "A member is closed. A member's items mean what they mean alone"; "The member's own answers, asked as a.q, are
# unchanged"; rows stated same are one movement, bound once (L §5.19 Bindings).  The migrator's F-k (t12/J): the
# member's def paid sums its own inh rows into sav; the joint states its own row fb[f1] (kind a.inh, same day, amount
# and places) same as a.sb[s1].  a.paid is the member's alone (100.00 DUK, a.m1 asked in M, sb[s1]'s amount carried
# through); the joint's binding over a.inh meets the one movement once (100.00 DUK); a.sav on 2025-10-01 books it
# once (100.00 DUK).  Before: a.paid 0.00 DUK (the member's binding bound the group by the joint's row, which the
# member doesn't see).
=== J/j.tally
model fam
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-15
  start 2025-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use a = "../M" sha256 "698df48002fc3a96782f72b267c71502d5dab16c627313160ff750729059a3da"

source fsrc "test"

input fb: observed

ask j1: a.paid, sum(o.cash.amount for o in a.inh over ..), bal(a.sav, 2025-10-01) law 2026-01-15 as known 2026-01-15

version f
  cite fsrc
  governs 2025-06..2025-12
  known 2026-01-15
  same fb[f1] = a.sb[s1]
  fb[f1] = (on: 2025-06-16, kind: a.inh, leg cash from a.world to a.sav amount 100.00 DUK) "f1"
=== M/m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-15
  start 2025-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source src "test"

unit DUK: currency minor 0.01

kind inh: transfers

place sav: accounts DUK lives 2025-01-01..

place world: outside lives 2000-01-01..

input sb: observed

def paid: money DUK = sum(o.cash.amount for o in inh over .. where o.cash.to == sav) at reader

ask m1: paid law 2026-01-15 as known 2026-01-15

version open
  cite src
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  opening[sav] = 0 at 2025-01-01 start

version s
  cite src
  governs 2025-06..2025-12
  known 2026-01-15
  covers sav
  anchor sav
  sb[s1] = (on: 2025-06-16, kind: inh, leg cash from world to sav amount 100.00 DUK) "s1"
  stated[sav] = 100.00 DUK at 2025-12-31 end "last"
=== expect
j1: (100.00 DUK, 100.00 DUK, 100.00 DUK)
  law date 2026-01-15, cut 2026-01-15
